What the mod overrides in vanilla CK3, so each can be re-checked after a CK3 patch.
Refreshed for 2.40 against vanilla 1.20.1.2 (WORK-ORDER-2.40 E3). Nothing needed re-basing for 1.20.1.2.
After each CK3 patch: list the vanilla files newer than the patch date and compare them with this list.

== 1. Whole vanilla files the mod ships a copy of (the mod's copy wins; a CK3 change to these never reaches players) ==

common > holdings > 00_holdings.txt, the entire file
2.39: vanilla's file with the Collegium (spn_order_collegium_01) added to the castle, city and church holdings. Copy it again from vanilla whenever a CK3 patch changes it.

common > on_action > child_birth_on_actions.txt, the entire file
on_birth_child calls spn_on_genetic_birth; the six pregnancy.* events are fired from spn_check_pregnancy instead.

common > scripted_effects > 00_intrigue_perk_effects.txt, the entire file
One OR adds bloodthirsty_perk.

common > scripted_modifiers > 00_perk_modifiers.txt, the entire file
One OR adds vampire_seduction_perk.

gui > window_situation_list.gui, the entire file
2.40 boot 2: vanilla's file plus the story focus for the HUD's pack, Order and coven buttons, and the Supernatural Trails
situation listed only for its watchers; changes marked "Supernatural 2.40". Regenerate from vanilla with
tool/pkgs/Q2/gen_situation_list.py whenever a CK3 patch changes it.

common > effect_localization > 00_perk_effects.txt, the entire file
Two added keys: master_shadows_perk_effect, unlocks_truce_purchasing_interaction_desc.

common > scripted_triggers > 00_lifestyle_triggers.txt, the entire file
Witchcraft and mod edits; 11 of its 13 triggers are identical to vanilla.

